,"categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"to","nome":"Tongan","termine":"papālagi","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"to","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Samoan papālagi, Tongan papālagi. Compare palagi."},{"parola":"pisupo","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"Canned corned beef.","termine_origine":"pisupo","catena":[{"codice":"sm","nome":"Samoan","termine":"pisupo","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"en","nome":"English","termine":"pea soup","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"en","ambiti":["cucina"],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from Samoan pisupo, from English pea soup. Pea soup was the first canned food introduced to Samoa, causing the islanders to refer to all canned foods as pisupo (a borrowing of pea soup adapted to the phonotactics of Samoan). Corned beef subsequently became the most common canned food in Sam"},{"parola":"Samoa","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"A kind of cookie with coconut flavoring, often sold by Girl Scouts.","termine_origine":"Sāmoa","catena":[{"codice":"sm","nome":"Samoan","termine":"Sāmoa","categoria":"prestito"}],"lontana":"sm","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from Samoan Sāmoa. See there for more."},{"parola":"saofai","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"In Samoan culture, the ceremony in which the title of matai (chief) is bestowed.","termine_origine":"saofai","catena":[{"codice":"sm","nome":"Samoan","termine":"saofai","categoria":"prestito"}],"lontana":"sm","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Samoan saofai."},{"parola":"sene","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":2,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"A unit of currency equivalent to a hundredth of a Samoan tala.","termine_origine":"sene","catena":[{"codice":"sm","nome":"Samoan","termine":"sene","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"en","nome":"English","termine":"cent","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"en","ambi